<title>USA: Hewlett-Packard signs hospital supply pact.</title>
<headline>Hewlett-Packard signs hospital supply pact.</headline>
<dateline>PALO ALTO, Calif. 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hewlett-Packard Co said Monday it had signed a three-year contract to supply patient-monitoring and resuscitation products to Premier Inc's hospital alliance.</p>
<p>The pact takes effect April 1 and is expected to be worth more than $300 million over the life of the contract.</p>
<p>Hewlett-Packard said the contract is its first with the new Premier group, a 1,800-member entity that emerged from the merger last year of American Healthcare Systems Inc, SunHealth Alliance Inc and Premier Health Alliance Inc.</p>
